{
  "id": "grammar.a2.20.04.futuro",
  "title": "Futuro Simple Review",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Use the *futuro* simple for predictions, expectations and future goals. Regular endings are attached to the full infinitive: *seguiré*, logrará, volveremos, empezarán. It can express what you expect will happen or what you intend to achieve in the future."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Seguiré estudiando español.",
          "english": "I will continue studying Spanish."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "El futuro será diferente.",
          "english": "The future will be different."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Lograremos nuestros objetivos.",
          "english": "We will achieve our goals."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Probablemente volverán algún día.",
          "english": "They will probably return someday."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "seguiré",
          "I will continue"
        ],
        [
          "será",
          "it will be"
        ],
        [
          "lograremos",
          "we will achieve"
        ],
        [
          "volverán",
          "they will return"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Ask what time frame you are describing. Use the pretérito perfecto for recent experiences, the indefinido for completed past events, ir a + infinitive for plans, and the *futuro* simple for predictions and future goals."
    },
    {
      "type": "external-link",
